From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:34:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: s2r: send the enclave no sleep request in
 a run set to abort

A bring-up run with abort_before set skips the coprocessors' last stops,
so that an abort never leaves one down without a sleep. The enclave's
sleep request was still sent: it gates the enclave, and only the power
cycle of a real sleep brings it back, so an aborted run left it asleep.

Send the request only when no abort is set. A run without it then finds
the enclave never told, as when an earlier refusal stops the sleep, which
the enclave's resume already handles.

abort_before is 0 by default; then nothing changes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
index 46dbf3005a..1415a5d71d 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/apple-s2r.c
@@ -41,7 +41,8 @@
  * apple_sleep_coproc_register(). Their last refusals and the enclave's sleep
  * request run first in ->enter(), before anything that can't be undone; then
  * their last stops, past every refusal. A bring-up run with abort_before set
- * stops none of them, so that an abort never leaves one down without a sleep.
+ * stops none of them and sends the enclave no request, so that an abort
+ * never leaves one down without a sleep.
  *
  * The SoC wakes the boot CPU at its reset vector. Boot firmware finds the
  * armed mailbox, redoes the boot CPU setup and branches to cpu_resume. After
@@ -496,7 +497,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(apple_sleep_coproc_stopped);
  * The last refusals: interrupts are off and no other CPU is up, so the
  * registry is read without its lock, which no one can hold now.
  */
-static int apple_s2r_coprocs_check(struct apple_s2r *s2r)
+static int apple_s2r_coprocs_check(struct apple_s2r *s2r, bool tell_enclave)
 {
 	int i, ret;
 
@@ -511,7 +512,7 @@ static int apple_s2r_coprocs_check(struct apple_s2r *s2r)
 			return ret;
 		}
 	}
-	if (apple_s2r_enclave.tell) {
+	if (tell_enclave && apple_s2r_enclave.tell) {
 		ret = apple_s2r_enclave.tell(apple_s2r_enclave.data);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err(s2r->dev, "refused: the enclave didn't take the sleep request: %d\n",
@@ -1015,8 +1016,12 @@ static int apple_s2r_enter(suspend_state_t state)
 	}
 	apple_s2r_crumb(s2r, S2R_CRUMB_ENTER);
 
-	/* The coprocessors' last refusals, before anything that can't be undone */
-	ret = apple_s2r_coprocs_check(s2r);
+	/*
+	 * The coprocessors' last refusals, before anything that can't be undone.
+	 * The enclave's sleep request gates it, and only the power cycle of a
+	 * real sleep brings it back: a run that aborts on purpose doesn't send it.
+	 */
+	ret = apple_s2r_coprocs_check(s2r, !READ_ONCE(abort_before));
 	if (ret) {
 		s2r->failed_step = S2R_STEP_COPROCS;
 		goto fail;
